---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import FieldDemo from "../../components/FieldDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Field"
  description="Labeled form rows: Field, ChoiceGroup, CheckboxField, FieldSeparator, and FieldsDisabled."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Field</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A labeled row for one form control, with a required or optional marker, a
    counter, and a helper or error line. ChoiceGroup and CheckboxField cover
    radios and checkboxes. FieldsDisabled locks a whole form while it saves.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><FieldDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Field usage"
      code={`import {
  CheckboxField,
  ChoiceGroup,
  Field,
  FieldSeparator,
  FieldsDisabled,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/field";
import { Input } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/input";

<FieldsDisabled value={saving}>
  <form noValidate onSubmit={save}>
    <Field label="Name" required error={errors.name}>
      <Input value={name} onChange={(event) => setName(event.target.value)} />
    </Field>
    <Field
      label="Instructions"
      required
      counter="120 / 8,000"
      helper="Tell the agent what to do."
    >
      <Textarea rows={4} maxLength={8000} />
    </Field>
    <ChoiceGroup
      type="radio"
      legend="Repeat"
      required
      layout="columns"
      options={[
        { value: "daily", label: "Every day", description: "Runs at 9:00 AM" },
        { value: "weekly", label: "Every week" },
      ]}
      value={repeat}
      onValueChange={setRepeat}
    />
    <CheckboxField
      label="Notify me when it runs"
      checked={notify}
      onCheckedChange={setNotify}
    />
    <FieldSeparator>or</FieldSeparator>
  </form>
</FieldsDisabled>`}
    />
    <p>
      Every Field, ChoiceGroup, and CheckboxField says whether it is
      <code>required</code> or <code>optional</code>; there is no default. The
      marker sits next to the label. Pass <code>id</code> to name the control, or
      leave it out to generate one.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Field</h2>
    <p>
      <code>label</code> names the control. <code>labelVisibility</code> is
      <code>"visible"</code> (default) or <code>"screen-reader"</code>, which
      keeps the label, marker, and counter for assistive tech only.
      <code>helper</code> is a line of help below the control.
      <code>error</code> replaces it and marks the control invalid.
      <code>counter</code> is short status at the end of the label row, such as
      <code>"120 / 8,000"</code>. <code>disabled</code> dims the label and disables
      the control.
    </p>
    <p>
      The child is one control, or one element that wraps it. Sprout
      <code>Input</code> and <code>SelectTrigger</code> join the field on their own.
      For any other control, call <code>useFieldControl(props)</code> and spread the
      result on the focusable element:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="useFieldControl"
      code={`function Textarea(rest: ComponentProps<"textarea">) {
  const props = useFieldControl(rest);
  return <textarea {...props} className="my-textarea" />;
}`}
    />
    <p>
      It adds the field's <code>id</code>, <code>disabled</code>,
      <code>aria-describedby</code>, <code>aria-invalid</code>, and
      <code>aria-required</code>. Outside a Field, or when the control has its
      own
      <code>aria-label</code> or <code>aria-labelledby</code>, props pass
      through unchanged.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">ChoiceGroup</h2>
    <p>
      <code>type="radio"</code> picks one value and <code>type="checkbox"</code>
      picks many. <code>options</code> are <code
        >{"{ value, label, description?, disabled? }"}</code
      >. <code>layout</code> is <code>"list"</code> (default) or
      <code>"columns"</code>, two columns from 640px. It also takes
      <code>legend</code>, <code>legendVisibility</code>, <code>helper</code>,
      <code>error</code>, <code>disabled</code>, <code>id</code>, and
      <code>warning</code>, a badge after the legend such as "Changes data".
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">CheckboxField</h2>
    <p>
      One checkbox with a label and a helper or error line. <code>variant</code>
      is <code>"default"</code>, filled with the primary color, or
      <code>"neutral"</code>, filled with the text color for filter lists. The
      <code>id</code> goes on the wrapper, so a form can scroll to it and focus the
      checkbox inside.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">FieldSeparator and FieldsDisabled</h2>
    <p>
      <code>FieldSeparator</code> is a labeled <code>Separator</code> that pulls in
      the stack gap, so the line sits evenly between fields. Text such as "or" is
      optional. <code>FieldsDisabled</code> is a context provider:
      <code>{"<FieldsDisabled value={saving}>"}</code> disables every field below
      it.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Labels point at their control with <code>for</code>. The control is
      described by the error or helper, then the optional marker, then the
      counter. Required controls get <code>aria-required</code>; invalid ones
      get
      <code>aria-invalid</code>. A checkbox group is a labelled
      <code>role="group"</code>; a radio group is a Base UI radiogroup with
      arrow key movement. Each option row is clickable, and option descriptions
      describe their checkbox or radio.
    </p>
    <p>
      Checkboxes and radios show a 2px focus ring. Rows are at least 36px tall,
      and 44px on touch screens. Colors change in 120ms and stop when reduced
      motion is requested. Forced colors mode uses system colors.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Labels use <code>--sprout-text</code>; markers, counters, and helpers use
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>; errors use <code>--sprout-danger</code>.
      Checked boxes use <code>--sprout-primary</code> and
      <code>--sprout-on-primary</code>, and checked rows use
      <code>--sprout-primary-subtle</code>. Focus rings use
      <code>--sprout-focus</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
